From 91beb9c525ea19725718f67a13faf714804daf37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:59:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Keep OpenSSL private macros out of raw assembly actions

The assembly_defines_test fails on production Windows GNU actions before the repair and passes afterwards, including a selected feature macro and private CcInfo scope. The combined build clears the unused-argument errors and exposes separate assembly flavor selection and Windows-only unused-helper defects. Full build, runtime, lock, and fresh emitted-patch acceptance remain pending.
---
